hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3004","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Yahya ibn Sa'id, narrated to us 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, narrated to us 'Ata', on the authority of Usamah ibn Zayd (RA) that he entered the House (the Ka'bah) along with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He (the Prophet (ﷺ)) commanded Bilal (RA) to close the door, and at that time the House had six columns. He (the Prophet (ﷺ)) proceeded until he reached the two pillars that stood next to the door of the Ka'bah, then he sat down. He praised Allah, extolled Him, supplicated to Him, and sought forgiveness from Him. Then he stood up and went to the rear part of the Ka'bah that faced away from the door, placed his face and body against the Ka'bah, praised Allah, extolled Him, and sought forgiveness from Allah. Then he turned to each corner of the Ka'bah, facing them with takbir (saying \Allahu Akbar\"")"","" tahlil (saying \""La ilaha illallah\"")"","" and tasbih (saying \""Subhanallah\"")"","" praising Allah"","" extolling Him with supplication and seeking forgiveness. Then he exited and prayed two rak'ahs facing the Ka'bah outside the House"","" and said: \""This is the qiblah"","" this is the qiblah.\""\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
"3005","Narrated to us Nasr ibn ‘Ali al-Jahdami: ‘Isa ibn Yunus informed us, on the authority of ‘Abd al-Malik al-‘Azrami.\n\nAnd narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Muhammad: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, who said: ‘Abd al-Malik narrated to us.\n\nAnd narrated to us al-Dawraqi: Hushaim informed us, on the authority of ‘Abd al-Malik.\n\nAnd narrated to us ‘Ali ibn al-Mundhir: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of ‘Abd al-Malik. They mentioned the hadith in its lengthy form, and sometimes they differed in a word or a detail.\n\nCHAPTER:"
